  "result": "I reviewed the diff and found a material defect: the new expression `items[len(items) - n:]` is **not** equivalent to the original `items[-n:]` outside the narrow range `0 < n <= len(items)`.\n\nTwo concrete breaks, both contradicting the PR's own stated requirement (\"must return the whole list when `n` exceeds its length, exactly as the slice did\"):\n\n- **`n = 0`**: old returns the whole list (`items[-0:]` == `items[0:]`); new returns `[]` (`items[len(items):]`).\n- **`n` just above `len(items)`** (e.g. `len=5, n=6`): old clamps to the whole list `[1,2,3,4,5]`; new gives `items[-1:]` \u2192 `[5]`, a single element instead of the full list \u2014 exactly the regression the PR claims to avoid.\n\nI wrote `review-payload.json` with `outcome: \"findings\"`, one `P0`/`must-fix`/blocking finding describing this, and a summary body suitable for publishing. No other files were modified and nothing was executed.",
